==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[hole in the wall]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[hole]]-in-the-[[wall]]|pl2=holes-in-the-wall}}

# a [[small]] or [[obscure]] [[place]], especially such a [[restaurant]]
# {{context|colloquial|chiefly|British|lang=en}} an [[automated teller machine]] (ATM)

====Usage notes====
Although either plural can be used for both meanings, ''[[hole-in-the-walls]]'' tends to be most commonly used for the "obscure place" sense, and ''[[holes-in-the-wall]]'' is more frequently used to mean "automated teller machines".

The British sense of an automated teller machine is a trademark of [[w:Barclays|Barclays]].